BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Heritage\, Harvest\, and Horse Festival
DTSTART:20261003T093000
DTEND:20261003T170000
DTSTAMP:20261003T150955Z
UID:1eff5442cebbf476c6b13a90a4a255@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Fort Ticonderoga\, surrounded by magnificent autumn backdrops 
 of the Adirondacks and Green Mountains will present the Annual Heritage\, 
 Harvest\, & Horse Festival on October 3\, 2026. The full day of autumn fun
  will be set in the midst of the King’s Garden heirloom apple trees and 
 the beautiful landscape of the mountains and Lake Champlain. Guests are in
 vited to discover the historical importance of horses and other working an
 imals during exciting demonstrations\, meet our friendly oxen duo\, stroll
  through Fort Ticonderoga’s farmers’ market featuring local food\, bev
 erages\, and crafts\, participate in family fun activities\, and tackle th
 e six-acre Heroic Corn Maze. This fall favorite event\, combined with dail
 y Fort Ticonderoga programs\, makes for a great annual family tradition. W
 hether you are looking to experience a horse-drawn wagon ride\, indulge in
  local homemade delights\, or pick apples by the bag from our heritage app
 le orchard\, there is something for everyone and all ages when it comes to
  our Annual Fall Festival! Confirmed vendors will be announced once we get
  closer. Heritage\, Harvest\, & Horse is included in your General Admissio
 n ticket!\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fort Ticonderoga\, 102 Fort Ti Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/heritage-h
 arvest-and-horse-festival-22-05-2026-11-24-03
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:IronPooch - Trail Race and Obstacle Course Challenge
DTSTART:20261003T100000
DTEND:20261003T140000
DTSTAMP:20261003T150955Z
UID:74e7c9f6f36a8e4f92b9e77b60040f@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The first IronPooch event will be hosted at Bolton Valley's Ti
 mberline Lodge on Oct 3\, 2026. Participants and their dogs can sign up to
  run or walk either a 5-mile or a 2-mile course\; both featuring multiple 
 agility obstacles. For the competitive runners\, the longer course will co
 nsist of a mix of steep and technical mountain trails\, while the shorter 
 course is designed to be approachable for everyone (and every breed!) of a
 ll ability levels. Not keen on racing? Not to worry - the base area will h
 ost an event worthy of a Fall morning on its own\, with live local music\,
  food & bev\, lots of great local vendors and sponsor tents\, and several 
 local 501c animal rescue organizations. These orgs will run adoption and f
 undraising drives via fun offerings including fur & paw treatments\, face 
 painting for kids\, and more. Come for the trails\, the tails\, or both! 7
 5\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Bolton Valley Resort\, 4302 Bolton Valley Access Rd
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/ironpooch-
 trail-race-and-obstacle-course-challenge-16-09-2026-11-32-24
END:VEVENT
